WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.273
Hi, I'm Tessellate!

00:00:02.273 --> 00:00:06.534
Comet sixty B is a smaller copy of an NVIDIA vision language model.

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:07.845
Here's what was cut.

00:00:09.808 --> 00:00:11.328
The idea: keep every layer.

00:00:11.328 --> 00:00:14.975
In each expert block, keep the half that matters most, narrow each

00:00:14.975 --> 00:00:16.495
one, and drop the rest.

00:00:18.717 --> 00:00:22.000
A token reaches a mixture of experts block, and a router scores

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.095
the experts for it.

00:00:23.515 --> 00:00:27.228
In the parent, it picks twenty-two of five hundred and twelve small networks.

00:00:27.648 --> 00:00:31.697
Comet keeps two hundred and fifty-six of them, and trims each one's hidden width.

00:00:32.117 --> 00:00:35.163
The router still picks twenty-two, so a token does about the

00:00:35.163 --> 00:00:36.271
same work as before.

00:00:38.275 --> 00:00:40.502
The model's own config names the method.

00:00:40.922 --> 00:00:44.658
Run sample text, images and video through it, and score each expert

00:00:44.658 --> 00:00:45.903
by what it adds.

00:00:46.323 --> 00:00:49.214
Drop the lowest scoring half, separately in every block.

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:53.520
Trim the weakest channels inside each survivor, and refit what is left.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:58.036
Then train it to copy the original model, and finish with reinforcement learning.

00:00:59.708 --> 00:01:03.379
Each router row is like a fingerprint for one expert, so matching

00:01:03.379 --> 00:01:04.909
them shows which ones survived.

00:01:05.329 --> 00:01:08.678
Every block keeps its own half, scattered, in the original order.

00:01:08.678 --> 00:01:10.504
No block keeps a neat range.

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:13.354
Stored parameters halve.

00:01:13.354 --> 00:01:19.052
But active parameters per token barely move, because each token still visits twenty-two experts.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.888
The cost shows up in vision.

00:01:22.888 --> 00:01:27.411
Sixteen of seventeen image and video scores fall, while agent scores mostly rise.

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:32.298
So pruning experts halves the memory a model like this needs, while

00:01:32.298 --> 00:01:34.652
the work per token stays almost the same.

00:01:36.692 --> 00:01:38.119
Half the experts kept.

00:01:38.119 --> 00:01:39.904
Memory halved, compute nearly unchanged.

00:01:39.904 --> 00:01:42.401
And vision pays most of the cost.

00:01:42.821 --> 00:01:44.948
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:44.948 --> 00:01:45.556
I'm Tessellate.

00:01:45.556 --> 00:01:45.860
Bye!
